<overview>
<p>Mechanized wheeled platoons transport their infantry in wheeled armored personnel carriers optimized for speed on roads and improved surfaces. Wheeled APCs are cheaper to maintain and faster on pavement than tracked alternatives, making these platoons ideal for garrison rapid-response forces, highway patrol, and urban security operations. Their off-road capability is limited compared to tracked vehicles, restricting employment in rough terrain, but on developed worlds with good road networks, wheeled mechanized infantry offer the best balance of speed, protection, and operating cost.</p><p>Towing crew-served light gauss rifles, these platoons trade the raw stopping power of full-size gauss weapons for improved mobility and a lighter logistics footprint, while still delivering magnetically accelerated rounds at ranges that exceed conventional autocannon.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as common/re-introduction date for Light Gauss Rifle field gun
</notes>

